3973 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 936 0 R
/T (Leader Election is a process used in distributed systems to select one process as the coordinator or leader. The Bully Algorithm is a leader-election algorithm in which each process has a unique ID. When a process detects that the current leader has failed, it sends election messages to processes with higher IDs. The highest active process eventually becomes the new leader and coordinates the system. )
/E (Leader Election is a process used in distributed systems to select one process as the coordinator or leader. The Bully Algorithm is a leader-election algorithm in which each process has a unique ID. When a process detects that the current leader has failed, it sends election messages to processes with higher IDs. The highest active process eventually becomes the new leader and coordinates the system. )
/Pg 115 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
