<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 939 0 R
/T (The /proc filesystem is a virtual filesystem in Linux that provides information about running processes and kernel data. Each running process has a directory named after its Process ID \(PID\). The /proc/[PID]/status file contains details such as process name, state and parent process ID \(PPID\). Python can read these files to monitor and display process information without directly modifying the kernel. )
/E (The /proc filesystem is a virtual filesystem in Linux that provides information about running processes and kernel data. Each running process has a directory named after its Process ID \(PID\). The /proc/[PID]/status file contains details such as process name, state and parent process ID \(PPID\). Python can read these files to monitor and display process information without directly modifying the kernel. )
/Pg 118 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
